# Greensleeves, melody with chords (repertoire plan: greensleeves-melody). A new arrangement of
# the anonymous Elizabethan tune: the first verse (A section, bars 1-8) and the refrain (B section,
# bars 9-16), one chord per bar as the plan gives them, with Am then E in bars 7 and 15.
# Your part is the tune in first position: G# on string 3 fret 1 (finger 1), A on string 3 fret 2
# (finger 2), E on string 4 fret 2, and the low F# on string 4 fret 4 (finger 4). The sixth note of
# the scale is F# throughout (the plan allows F or F#; this keeps it the same everywhere, as the
# fingerstyle arrangement does). The teacher strums each chord on the two dotted-quarter beats.
# Shapes: Am x02210, G 320003, E 022100, C x32010.
title: Greensleeves (melody)
